-- title:
--   Igusa reading of the second special-fibre component via σ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K\subseteq L((q))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of $\mathrm{jq}=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral power series})$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1\colon C_1\to\operatorname{Spec}k$, $c_2\colon C_2\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, equipped with closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ over $k$ into the base change to $k$ of the two-chart model $\mathrm{modelTo}\,A\,K\,j$ (the pushout of the charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, over $\operatorname{Spec}A$), whose images jointly cover that base change, with $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ reduced of cardinality $n>0$. Further data: a section $\varepsilon$ of the model over $\operatorname{Spec}A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change of $\varepsilon$; an integral weight-one form $w$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion, whose reduction in $k$ is nonzero); a curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ over $k$ of the Igusa field $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w=k\text{-}\mathrm{adjoin}$ of the $q$-expansion field of $X_1(M)$ over $k$ and the inverse of the reduced series of $w$, an isomorphism $e_1\colon \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C\cong C_1$ with $e_1$ followed by $c_1$ equal to $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, nonemptiness of the preimage in $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.C$ of the $j$-finite chart open, and the Gauss reading hypothesis: for every $a$ integral over $A[j]$ in $K$ and all $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero image in $k[[q]]$ and $a\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$, the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ along $e_1$ followed by $i_1$ and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$, transported into the Igusa field by $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, has Laurent series $\bar x/\bar y$ over $k$. Finally let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with $\sigma(j)$ of Laurent series $\mathrm{jq}(q^{p})$, preserving membership in the integral closure of $A[j]$, and such that for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ consisting exactly of the quotients $x/y$ with $x,y\in A[[q]]$ and $\bar y\neq0$, the comap $\sigma^{*}W_0$ differs from $W_0$ and contains $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P\in A[X]$ of nonzero reduction. Then for every integral weight-one form $w_2$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ there exist a curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ over $k$ of $\mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,k\,M\,w_2$, an isomorphism $e_2\colon\mathrm{Mdl}_2.C\cong C_2$ with $e_2$ followed by $c_2$ equal to $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{toBase}$, and nonemptiness of the preimage of the $j$-finite chart open, such that for every $a$ integral over $A[j]$ in $K$ and all $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with nonzero image of $y$ in $k[[q]]$ and $\sigma(a)\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$, the corresponding germ of $a$ along $e_2$ followed by $i_2$ and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$, transported into the Igusa field by $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, has Laurent series $\bar x/\bar y$ over $k$.
--
--   This identifies the second component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart stable model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$ with a model of the Igusa function field in characteristic $p$, the identification being pinned by $q$-expansions twisted by the level-$p$ automorphism $\sigma$ with $\sigma(j)=j(q^{p})$: chart functions read on this component as the reductions of the Gauss presentations of their $\sigma$-translates, mirroring the untwisted reading on the first component. It feeds the analysis of Hecke operators on the two components of the special fibre.
